write('investigations','Unanswered SIR questions','The outstanding questions about SIR decisions, forms and registration outcomes.', '<header class="article-top"><p class="eyebrow">SIR / UNANSWERED QUESTIONS</p><h1>What remains unanswered.</h1><p class="lede">These questions require the underlying orders, decisions and roll entries.</p></header><article class="prose">'+''.join('<section id="'+g['id']+'"><h2>'+E('Local registration outcomes' if g['id']=='G14' else g['topic'])+'</h2><p>'+E(g['needed'])+'</p></section>' for g in D['gap_register'])+'</article>')

# Delhi schedule history and intake are presented beside the local account.
p=R/'state-files/delhi/index.html';t=p.read_text();section='<h2 id="schedule-history">How Delhi’s timetable changed</h2><p>The dates below belong to older signed orders. They are not current deadlines. The district website lists the August letter under 19 September; its signed header is dated 19 August. The July bundle also differs internally: the CEO forwarding subject refers to 1 October as qualifying date, while the attached ECI subject says 1 July. The effect on actual decisions is not established.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Order</th><th>Draft target</th><th>Claims to</th><th>Disposal to</th><th>Final target</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>15 July</td><td>17 August</td><td>16 September</td><td>15 October</td><td>19 October</td></tr><tr><td>19 August</td><td>31 August</td><td>30 September</td><td>29 October</td><td>4 November</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Later September directions and the indexed 17 October CEO note give 30 October for claims. The latest signed replacement schedule is still required before treating every later target as authenticated. <a href="../../evidence/#DELHI-JUL15">July order</a> · <a href="../../evidence/#DELHI-AUG19">August order</a> · <a href="../../evidence/#DELHI-OCT17">October statement</a></p>'+delhi('../../')
if 'id="schedule-history"' not in t:t=t.replace('<h2 id="gaps">',section+'<h2 id="gaps">',1)
p.write_text(t)
# Explain the operative safeguards within existing procedure pages, not a new navigation route.
ssr_text='<section id="ssr-safeguards"><h2>What the 15 October SSR order requires</h2><p>These directions apply to the 17 scheduled SSR jurisdictions. They are not proof of compliance, nor an automatic replacement timetable for Delhi.</p><h3>Before a decision</h3><p>Paragraph 13 sets display and waiting-period requirements, including seven clear days after the required publication and sharing with political parties. It also requires personal notice for proposed deletions other than death cases and an opportunity to be heard where the stated procedure applies.</p><h3>Personal cross-checks</h3><p>Paragraph 20(b) requires the ERO personally to cross-check cases where deletions exceed 2% of a polling station’s electors, or the same person objects in more than five cases. These are checking triggers. They do not authorise a quota of deletions or replace the individual filing limits.</p><h3>Readable copies</h3><p>Paragraph 23(c)(ii) requires a free hard copy and readable PDF, without elector photographs, for recognised parties after draft and final publication. It does not promise an unrestricted public CSV or API.</p><h3>Appeals</h3><p>Paragraph 19 identifies the District Magistrate as first appellate authority and the CEO as second, under section 24 and rule 27. A particular appeal still needs the applicable instructions and order/service dates.</p><p><a href="../evidence/#ECI-SSR-OCT15">SSR order, paragraphs 13, 19, 20(b) and 23(c)(ii)</a></p></section>'
for relative in ['forms/index.html','restoration-and-ssr/index.html']:
 p=R/relative;t=p.read_text()
 if 'id="ssr-safeguards"' not in t:t=t.replace('</article>',ssr_text+'</article>',1)
 p.write_text(t)
p=R/'form-7/index.html';t=p.read_text();block='<section id="ssr-cross-checks"><h2>Filing limits and checking triggers are different</h2><p>The 15 October SSR order separately requires personal ERO cross-checks when deletions exceed 2% at a polling station or the same person is the objector in more than five cases. The more-than-five trigger is not a five-application filing limit. It is an extra checking requirement. <a href="../evidence/#ECI-SSR-OCT15">Paragraph 20(b)</a></p></section>'
if 'id="ssr-cross-checks"' not in t:t=t.replace('</article>',block+'</article>',1)
p.write_text(t)
